I kept delaying learning this because recursion and nested state updates felt overwhelming. But you explained it so well — finally got it now! 🙌 Been following you since 2019, You make every concept easy to understand.Thank you!

Just a heads-up — there's an edge case. If a parent has both leaf and nested children (like Apple, Banana, and Citrus under Fruits), checking all of Citrus’s children doesn’t check Citrus if Apple or Banana are unchecked.
If I check only Orange and Lemon, Citrus doesn’t get marked as checked.
That’s because .every() short-circuits — when it hits Apple or Banana and sees they’re unchecked, it immediately returns false and skips checking the rest like Citrus.

To fix it, replace verifyChecked with:

const verifyChecked = (node) => {
        if (!node.children || node.children.length === 0) {
          return newState[node.id] || false;
        }
        const areAllChildrenChecked = node.children.map((data) =>
          verifyChecked(data)
        );
        const areAllChecked = areAllChildrenChecked.every(Boolean);
        newState[node.id] = areAllChecked;
        return areAllChecked;
 };
